   "SECTION_NUMBER": "Para 22",
   "SECTION_TITLE": "Transaction Monitoring",
   "CHUNK_TEXT": "Banks shall put in place a robust transaction monitoring system capable of identifying, on a risk-based approach, transactions that appear suspicious. The monitoring system shall flag transactions based on velocity, amount, geography, and counterparty risk. Alerts generated shall be reviewed by a qualified compliance officer. Banks shall maintain records of all monitoring alerts and their disposition for a minimum period of 5 years.",
